{
  "name": "TeamRetro: Turn standup blockers into Jira issues and follow them until they clear",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "tr1900-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -400,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## TeamRetro: Turn standup blockers into Jira issues and follow them until they clear\n\nFor engineering managers whose standup blockers get said once and lost. When a TeamRetro standup closes, OpenAI triages each new blocker and the actionable ones become Jira issues. A blocker carried into later standups is matched back to its issue, and once it has been open `staleAfter` standups the issue gets a comment, and again every `staleAfter` standups after that.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. The TeamRetro Trigger fires on **Standup Completed**. A delivery TeamRetro retries is skipped, so nothing happens twice.\n2. Each update under your blocker question becomes one item, split into new and carried over.\n3. **New:** OpenAI returns whether it is actionable, a category and an issue title. Actionable ones become Jira issues, are remembered in the `standup_blockers` Data Table, and are announced in Slack.\n4. **Carried over:** the Data Table finds the issue, moves it to today's update, and comments on Jira when the blocker is overdue.\n\n### Setup\n\n- [ ] Create a Data Table named `standup_blockers` with columns: updateId, issueKey (strings)\n- [ ] Copy the Production URL from \"When Standup Closes\" into TeamRetro under Settings → Integrations → Webhooks, tick **Standup Completed**, and paste the signing secret back into the trigger\n- [ ] Set `jiraUrl`, `teamChannel` and `staleAfter` in \"Settings\"\n- [ ] Connect OpenAI, Jira and Slack, and pick the Jira project and issue type\n\nSample data is pinned. Running the pinned sample a second time stops at \"Skip Repeat Deliveries\": that is the duplicate guard.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdd labels or a priority under Additional Fields on \"Create the Jira Issue\".",
        "height": 710,
        "width": 720
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1900-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
